	    documentation 	
|Example Interface for an unary operation with 'this' as the only Argument.
| * This interface is not very usable, because the Operation Name 'Operation' 
| * carries no Semantics so it is hard to read and understand.
| * Rather use specific Operations, give them an understandable Name 
| * and define a new Interface for them, modeled after this one. 
| * 
| * Design Decisions:
| 
	    
	    stereotype 	"Interface"
	    operations 	(list Operations
		(object Operation "Operation"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
			(object Attribute
			    tool       	"Java"
			    name       	"Abstract"
			    value      	TRUE))
		    quid       	"37BD38310101"
		    documentation 	
|This is the Template for a reserved Operation working on an Object.
|	 * The Class brings along the Meaning for this Operation.
|	 
		    
		    result     	"void"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0))
	    module     	"Component View::intTest::operable"
	    quidu      	"36BC68820371"
	    language   	"Java")
